# ARX-01 - Open-Source Optical Communications Receiver Front End

**ARX-01 is an open-source optical communications receiver front end designed for Pulse Position Modulation (PPM) and On-Off Keying (OOK) free-space optical communication systems.**

The project is intended to make practical optical communications hardware accessible to researchers, engineers, students, amateur experimenters, and developers working on photon-limited optical links, satellite communications, and communications in RF-denied or RF-congested environments.

This repository contains the ARX-01 receiver hardware documentation, PCB manufacturing files, bill of materials, assembly information, and preliminary datasheet.

## Overview

Free-space optical communication uses modulated light instead of radio-frequency energy to transfer information between two locations.

Optical links can be useful where:

* RF spectrum is congested
* RF operation is restricted or undesirable
* Directional communications are beneficial
* High link directivity is required
* Photon-efficient communications are important
* Experimental satellite or space communications are being developed
* A license-free optical physical layer is desirable, subject to applicable local safety and regulatory requirements

ARX-01 is being developed as an **open-source optical receiver / analog front end** for these applications.

The receiver is intended to support optical communication waveforms including:

* **Pulse Position Modulation (PPM)**
* **On-Off Keying (OOK)**

PPM is particularly attractive for photon-limited optical communication because transmitted optical energy can be concentrated into relatively short pulses while information is encoded in the position of those pulses.

## Applications

Possible applications for ARX-01 include:

* Free-space optical communications
* Laser communications
* LED optical communications
* PPM optical communication experiments
* OOK optical communication experiments
* Satellite optical communications
* Ground-to-space optical links
* Space-to-ground optical links
* Inter-platform optical communications
* Photon-limited communication experiments
* Radio-denied communications
* RF-congested environments
* University and laboratory research
* Amateur optical communication experimentation
* Optical modem and communication-system development

## ARX-01

ARX-01 is the optical receiver front end in this project.

The hardware is intended to receive a modulated optical signal and provide an electrical signal suitable for subsequent detection, demodulation, timing recovery, or digital processing.

For current electrical, optical, and performance specifications, see:

**[`ARX-01_Preliminary_Datasheet.pdf`](ARX-01_Preliminary_Datasheet.pdf)**

The datasheet should be considered the authoritative source for the current ARX-01 hardware specifications.

