## Research and Experimental Use

ARX-01 is open hardware intended for experimentation, development, and research.

Performance of a complete optical communications link depends on the transmitter, receiver, optics, environment, implementation, and operating conditions.

Users should independently verify that the hardware is suitable for their application.

## Optical and Laser Safety

**Always follow appropriate optical and laser safety practices.**

Invisible infrared radiation can be particularly hazardous because the human eye may not provide a visible warning or normal blink response.

The ARX-01 receiver itself is only one part of an optical communications system; optical transmitters used with it may present eye or equipment hazards.

Users are responsible for appropriate safety analysis, laser classification, operating procedures, and compliance with applicable regulations.

